-- title:
--   #Lop-AE-SparseTri in time O(n² log²D / D^0.0703531 + w D^0.4296471 log D + nD + w) when D^1249 ≤ n^71
-- statement:
--   There are a constant $C$ and a time function $T(n,D,w)$ such that the counting version of Lop-AE-SparseTri (`lopCountTask`: given the $0/1$ biadjacency matrices of a lopsided graph with $n$ outer and $D$ inner vertices and $w$ query pairs $(a,b)$, write for each pair the number of common neighbours) is solved in time $T$ (`LopSolvedIn`: by one program of the light language with a polynomially bounded need, with time at most $T(n,D,w')$ whenever $w\le w'$), and for all $n,D,w$ with $2\le D$ and $D^{1249}\le n^{71}$
--   $$T(n,D,w)\le C\Big(\frac{n^2\log^2D}{D^{0.0703531}}+wD^{0.4296471}\log D+nD+w+1\Big).$$
--
--   This is the thin product with pruned encodings at $c=21.2733$, $\theta=0.111731$ (`allInstancesF_programF`), applied to the biadjacency matrices; $0.0703531<\Gamma$ and $0.4296471>q$ are the rounded exponents of Lemma 5.1.
-- source:
--   Developed for the prove2.me APSP exponent campaign (https://prove2.me/campaigns/apsp-exponent) on top of the Lean formalization anthropics/formal-math, folder 3sum-apsp, commit e1a4e65 (https://github.com/anthropics/formal-math/tree/e1a4e6508154ea59f030480661590a9fe3018011/3sum-apsp; Lean v4.33.1, Mathlib v4.33.1). The statement comes from the file 3sum-apsp/ThreeSumApsp/Filter/ThinLop.lean of the campaign's modified copy of that library, which is not published; the new definitions it uses are in the platform definition bundles APSP2996001_Defs1 and APSP2996001_Defs2 (and APSP299791_Defs1 to APSP299791_Defs5 of the 2.99791 entry). It follows the technical note "Deterministic APSP via thin products" (6 October 2026) refining J. Alman and V. Vassilevska Williams, "Truly Subquadratic 3SUM and Truly Subcubic APSP via Triangles in Sparse Lopsided Graphs", arXiv:2610.06783v1 (https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.06783v1), Lemma 5.1.

